      {
        "id": 32457,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-04T19:48:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Rabit&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Rabit\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Tamar\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/85f322/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Tamar:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[quote=“Rabit”]For those interested, the author was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Rothfuss\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Patrick Rothfuss</a> (of <span class=\"bbcode-i\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Kingkiller_Chronicle\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Kingkiller Chronicle</a></span> fame. Christopher was really stoked to talk to him, as he’s a fan. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And how!  I’m surprised he didn’t melt into a little puddle of fan squee <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> (Like I pretty much did when I got to talk to Gail Simone once OMGOMGOMG)[/quote]</p>\n<p>Oh, the look on Christopher’s face when he pointed Patrick out to me the second time he wandered by was absolutely adorable…  He didn’t quite melt, but it was pretty close. ;D</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Neat.  There aren’t that many authors that I follow for long.  I was pretty jazzed when I met R.A. Salvatore.  It was at a really small book signing in College Station, TX, so we actually just hung out and BS-ed for like an hour.  I wouldn’t mind meeting Margaret Weis and Tracy Hickman, or maybe Stephen King, but otherwise, I rarely read more than 2-3 books by the same author.  (Well, ok, Robert Jordan, but I’ll never meet him).</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:06:25.148Z",
