      {
        "id": 32465,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-04T21:34:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;arenson9&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"arenson9\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"broccoli\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/48/1861_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> broccoli:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Alas, I can usually only make one Con each year, and that’s usually BGG Con.  That plus an annual deer hunting trip and a quasi-annual family vacation usually eat most of my vacation time.  Combine that with living smack-dab in the middle of Texas means that any of the majors (Pax Prime, Pax East, Gen Con) are air-fare required.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What’s BGG Con? Ever considerd going to Owlcon in Houston?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>As far as college-based cons go, I usually hit AggieCon instead (held at Texas A&amp;M, my alma mater).  I guess I should have included that one in my list, but it’s relatively small, especially since its home (the MSC) has been under remodeling the past several years.  I realize that BGG Con may not have the biggest attendance out there, but it’s extremely focused, so it seems “bigger” because the parts I care most about (board games are card games) are the whole thing.</p>",
