      {
        "id": 32467,
        "name": "Tamar",
        "username": "Tamar",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/85f322/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-05T13:51:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;broccoli&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"broccoli\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Neat.  There aren’t that many authors that I follow for long.  I was pretty jazzed when I met R.A. Salvatore.  It was at a really small book signing in College Station, TX, so we actually just hung out and BS-ed for like an hour.  I wouldn’t mind meeting Margaret Weis and Tracy Hickman, or maybe Stephen King, but otherwise, I rarely read more than 2-3 books by the same author.  (Well, ok, Robert Jordan, but I’ll never meet him).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>At WisCon a couple of years ago I was at an academic paper reading/discussion and, as we were walking out, the woman I’d been sitting next to and chatting with introduced herself.  Turned out I’d just been chilling with Tamora Pierce.  She’s a lovely lady, btw <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
